From 95dcd905b04765c77cd55c3361e155855be6bc01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 21:42:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] aarch64_fuzz: pin -ffp-contract=off; the 12 O2 'mismatches'
 were false positives

The differential harness compared bitwise output of FP kernels compiled by
lccc-arm and aarch64-gcc without pinning FP contraction. GCC defaults to
-ffp-contract=fast on aarch64, and both compilers may legally contract
a*b+c chains into fmadd at different points, giving standard-conforming
but bitwise-different results (seed 25: the fa[i]=fs feedback loop
amplifies one 0.5-ulp rounding difference into full hash divergence;
verified: gcc -ffp-contract=off output == lccc output bit-for-bit).

Root-cause evidence: recompiling the failing seed-25 objects with
-ffp-contract=off made lccc and gcc byte-identical (aec79caa both);
lccc emits no fmadd for the kernel, gcc does. All 12 remaining O2
mismatches were this class (scen 0/2 FP-array kernels).

With contraction pinned, sweep extended to seeds 0:100 at O1/O2/Os =
300/300 clean. lccc's own contraction behaviour stays covered by the
fp-contract matrix regression (off/default/fast-math -> 0/1/0 fmadd).
